bbapprove help token — where the API token comes from.

Resolved in this order:
  1. BBAPPROVE_TOKEN, when set and non-empty. It wins; 1Password is not consulted.
  2. The 1Password item named by --token-name NAME, BBAPPROVE_TOKEN_NAME or user_token_name (that precedence),
     looked up with: op item get NAME --reveal --fields label=token, then label=credential if that fails
     or is empty. There is no default item name.
  3. Neither: every run that talks to the forge (dry run, --apply, -i) stops at once with exit 1, before the
     adapter is called. --help, --print-config, --init, --outdated, --update and doctor need no token;
     doctor flags a missing source as a problem and never looks the item up.

Create a Bitbucket Server / Data Center HTTP access token for the account that reviews the PRs: repository read
access (dashboard, build status, PR details) plus write access to approve, merge, comment on and decline.

There is no --token option: a token on the command line is visible in the process list and shell history.
